  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women and Migrant Families:  Establishing a base in which to replicate a successful SJM project.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project Women and Migrant Families aims to strengthen women headed households in which the husbands, and often male children, have emigrated.  It has three elements:  establishing mutual peer support groups for the women; training in managing the remittances they receive through community banks; encouraging small enterprise to enable the women to increase their income and savings.  This experience was implemented by the SJM over 3 years in the Diocese of S. Andr&#xe9;s Tuxtla, with very positive outcomes.  SJM plan to replicate the experience in other dioceses in Mexico.  This grant will allow the SJM to research and identify a suitable location.  This exploratory phase will involve statistical research, studies of the latest census, local surveys, interviews, defining selection criteria and utlimately identifying a location in which to implement a 3 year repetition of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
